LICENSE: NOT YET CHOSEN

No license has been granted yet. All rights reserved by the author until a
license is picked. This file is a placeholder for that decision.

Common choices for a small browser add-on, for when it is published:
- MIT: shortest permissive license; anyone may reuse, including in closed
  forks. Most common for userscripts and small extensions.
- MPL-2.0: Mozilla's license; changes to these files must stay open, but they
  can be combined with other code. Natural fit for a Firefox add-on.
- GPL-3.0: any redistributed derivative must be fully open source under GPL.

AMO asks for a license when an add-on is listed publicly. Unlisted (private)
signing does not need one.
